=== minutes, decomposed: what could be known and what could be had.
Baseline is the shipped model. Positive means hindsight gains, so each
mean is an upper bound. The three oracled arms are NESTED:
  availability  a season total of zero minutes — never played at all
  lineups       who is picked over the window, priced at conditional averages
  minutes       the realised minutes themselves
The subtraction is the point: lineups is the REACHABLE part, and
minutes minus lineups is the residual nobody could have bought.
They declare no cell invariance — they move everything legitimately —
so the mediators below are the only proof the arms are not inert.

CONDITIONAL PRICES — what the lineups arm pays per state, in minutes.
A start is most of a match; a substitute appearance is 15-25 minutes and
must not reach sixty, where appearance points and the clean sheet step.
'recon' is the share of club-gameweeks whose `starts` this parser inferred
from minutes: usable in aggregate, explicitly not as individual evidence.
